d diapers on the shelves  the supply chain issues were causing a  big a big problem and if they were able  to to find the diapers they couldn't  afford them they were out of work  waiting for unemployment 11 12 weeks so  we launched a diaper bank we helped 63  families the first week oh my gosh  congratulations and now  so in november we celebrated 1 million  diapers 3 million wipes to over 18 000  southern nevadans that is absolutely  incredible and i feel like you guys are  only just getting started let's talk  about what's new in 2022 we're so  excited so our long-term goal was to  create a mobile diaper bank  we were noticing that our clients  were experiencing transportation issues  so we wanted to solve the transportation  problem for them so  we had an amazing year and with some  great community support we just placed  an order for a mobile diaper bank oh my  gosh congratulations i think that's  going to make a huge difference in our  community and we're also just showing  some photos on the screen there of the  community really coming together in  support how does it feel to know that  you know you're going into the 13th year  that you're continuing to make a  difference in lives and families who  really need it sure well i'm a local  born and raised  it's the greatest honor of my lifetime  to be able to help my community on this  scale so we're going to continue to  support families in need in southern  nevada  we're going to solve diaper need in  southern nevada by 2025  and we're going to start with this  mobile diaper bank well congratulations  i think 2022 is going to be your guys  year and if people want to get involved  or help or need your assistance where do  they go babiesbounty.org they can find  all the ways to help we have volunteer  opportunities there's donation  opportunities  folks prefer to donate cash it's easier  for them we have that portal on our  website  we always accept new unopened diapers as  long as um they're size four five and  